q 0.820 0.860 0.920 RG 0.80 w 0.980 0.980 0.990 rg 40.00 360.00 515.00 138.00 re B Q
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.120 0.250 0.480 rg 48.00 484.00 Td (A. Traversal Ownership Trade-off \(Visitor-Managed vs. Element-Managed\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.8 Tf 0.200 0.200 0.250 rg 52.00 472.00 Td (* Visitor-Managed Traversal \(Selected\): Traversal is controlled in visit\(DirectoryNode\). This grants individual visitors the) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.8 Tf 0.200 0.200 0.250 rg 52.00 461.00 Td (  autonomy to control search ordering, depth stacks, and path segments, keeping node elements lightweight and unburdened.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.8 Tf 0.200 0.200 0.250 rg 52.00 450.00 Td (* Element-Managed Traversal \(Alternative\): Having DirectoryNode.accept recurse over children forces a single uniform traversal) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.8 Tf 0.200 0.200 0.250 rg 52.00 439.00 Td (  strategy onto all operations, depriving visitors of specialized pre/post-order actions or path tracking.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.120 0.250 0.480 rg 48.00 423.00 Td (B. The Visitor Pattern Dual Trade-off \(Operations vs. Element Types\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.8 Tf 0.200 0.200 0.250 rg 52.00 411.00 Td (* Adding New Operations \(Easy / Open-Closed\): New visitor classes \(e.g., StatisticsVisitor\) are added without modifying) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.8 Tf 0.200 0.200 0.250 rg 52.00 400.00 Td (  existing classes \(FileNode, DirectoryNode, Element, or other visitors\). The extension boundary is the Visitor interface.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.8 Tf 0.200 0.200 0.250 rg 52.00 389.00 Td (* Adding New Elements \(Hard / Element Rigidity\): Introducing a new element \(e.g., SymlinkNode\) breaks the Visitor interface,) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.8 Tf 0.200 0.200 0.250 rg 52.00 378.00 Td (  requiring a new visit\(SymlinkNode\) method and forcing modifications across every existing concrete visitor in the codebase.) Tj ET
